invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: sha512_test_host
reason: majority joins a ^ b and b ^ c with OR where the three-operation
  form of FIPS 180-4's equation 4.9 joins them with AND, so where a and b
  differ it returns the complement of b whatever c is, every round's T2
  is wrong, and so is every digest a host object computes under the
  library's own names. bin/sha512_test_host runs FIPS 180-4's SHA-384 and
  SHA-512 examples and RFC 6234's million-byte message on that path, and
  the first vector fails.

--- old
    return b ^ (a_xor_b & b_xor_c);
--- new
    return b ^ (a_xor_b | b_xor_c);
